- namespace
- lain_peek
- lain_poke

' A trusted published operation can do a check of a complete read-set and plan
' more than one write against one namespace snapshot. The supervisor does not
' yield to another request while it admits the plan. Ordinary record ops stay
' valid.
+ namespace_op
  : plan={\ path myth namespace}either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]

+ namespace_command
  + plan
    \ target=path operation=path input=myth state=namespace
    ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    ? !(state.permitted(target)) (./err 'write_outside_authority)
    ?> (./some record) (sovereign_care .x operation state).fil
      | ./err 'warp_op_unknown
    ?> (./some held) record.get(system_vocabulary/op)
      | ./err 'warp_op_bad
    ? held
     > command=namespace_op
      = plan command.plan
      | plan target input state
     > ordinary=op
      | ./ok [[target (writ/warp operation input)]]
    | ./err 'warp_op_bad

  + run
    ' One submitted event can cause a maximum of 128 reaction rounds. This is
    ' the shared admission budget for supervisor writes and installed
    ' operations. The budget is a limit on rounds. It is not a limit on
    ' arbitrary work done in a native hand. Only a quiescent candidate that
    ' has no outbound effects can be committed.
    \ command=task now=nat block=nat state=namespace index=hive
    ^ either[iota [namespace hive]]
    = [result next_index] (sovereign_cycle_with index command 0 128 now block state)
    ? result
     > (./fail why) (./err why)
     > (./spun next moves rounds ack spill)
      ? spill
       > (./some why) (./err why)
      ? moves.len (./err 'outbound_not_supported)
      | ./ok [next next_index]
  + admit
    ' The plan and the reactions see one immutable candidate. If this function
    ' does not admit the plan, it publishes no candidate.
    \ plan={\ namespace}either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]] state=namespace index=hive
    ^ either[iota [namespace hive]]
    = nobody=path []
    | namespace_command/admit_by nobody plan state index
  + admit_by
    ' This function does the same for a foot. by is the path where the foot is
    ' registered, and the journal keeps by. If by is empty, there is no foot,
    ' and the caller is a trusted caller in the world.
    \ by=path plan={\ namespace}either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]] state=namespace index=hive
    ^ either[iota [namespace hive]]
    ?> (./ok planned) (Try plan state) (./err 'command_plan_failed)
    < writes planned
    ? !(writes.len) (./ok [state index])
    ? (eq by.len 0) (namespace_command/run (task/vines writes) 0 0 state index)
    | namespace_command/run (task/sent by writes) 0 0 state index
